<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sō Yoshitoshi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1568">1568</a>–<a href="/years/1615">1615</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as So Yoshitoshi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sō Yoshitoshi was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of Tsushima and head of the Sō clan, which managed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. He acted as go-between before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>'s invasions of Korea in 1592, served in them, and afterwards negotiated the restoration of relations, concluded in the Treaty of Kiyu of 1609.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/so-yoshitoshi.jpg" alt="Sō Yoshitoshi" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C5%8D_Yoshitoshi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
